Q:
Find the following limit using either forms or continuity: lim as x -> 1^+ of (1-x)^(-3)

A:
-infinity

lim as x -> 1^+ of (1-x)^(-3) = lim as x -> 1^+ of 1/(1-x)^3.

As x -> 1^+, (1-x)^3 -> (0^-)^3 = 0^-.

Form is 1/0^- which approaches -infinity.

Thus lim as x -> 1^+ of (1-x)^(-3) = -infinity.

